    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d85ab2a_028ae715",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/NsdService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 463,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-16T08:43:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, thanks for the explanation.\n\nIf `RemoteException` it\u0027s the netd process that crashed, right ? In that case the system is restarting. We don\u0027t have to send a callback at all, the device is rebooting immediately anyway.\n\nIf resolution wasn\u0027t in progress, then yes your suggestion makes sense. Ideally, you\u0027d have three different errors :\nFAILURE_RESOLUTION_NOT_STARTED\nFAILURE_RESOLUTION_ALREADY_SUCCEEDED\nFAILURE_RESOLUTION_ALREADY_STOPPED\n\nBut if you can\u0027t distinguish, then RESOLUTION_NOT_RUNNING is fine for all three cases.",
      "parentUuid": "5f36c732_02c027f5",
